---
title: "programmable_tx_price_update (Pyth Sui Price Feeds: Use Real-Time Data)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_upgrade: resolve latest Pyth package address
    q_check_upgrade --> q_call_update: pyth::update_single_price_feed(latest_package, vaa_data)
    q_call_update --> q_verify: on-chain Wormhole VAA verification
    q_verify --> q_abort: VAA verification failed
    q_abort --> [*]: abort (invalid price update)
    q_verify --> q_store: VAA verification passed
    q_store --> q_consume: PriceInfoObject updated on-chain
    q_consume --> q_user_call: user_contract::function(PriceInfoObject)
    q_user_call --> [*]: return result

    note right of q_check_upgrade
        INV-001: Must call update_single_price_feed from client-side only (not hardcoded in Move)
        INV-002: Hardcoded call-site will brick on Pyth package upgrade
        INV-003: Pyth only allows interaction with the most recent package version
    end note

    note right of q_verify
        INV-004: Wormhole VAA must be cryptographically valid
        INV-005: Price data must originate from authorized Pyth publishers
    end note

    note right of q_consume
        INV-006: User contract must call pyth::get_price on PriceInfoObject (not update)
        INV-007: Programmable transaction ensures atomicity of update + consume
    end note
